---
import Article from '../../../../layouts/Article.astro';
import r from '../../../../data/signal_revenue_example.json';
---
<Article
  title="Why was retail revenue £81,948 higher on 20 September 2011?"
  description="Recalculate one historical Signal Lab revenue alert from the released daily totals and weekday baseline."
  path="/projects/signal-lab/investigate/"
  eyebrow="Signal Lab · worked investigation"
  heading="Why was retail revenue higher on 20 September 2011?"
  back={{ label: 'Signal Lab case study', href: '/projects/signal-lab/' }}
>
<div class="investigation">

  
  <p id="missing-alert" hidden>This example has no record for the requested alert. <a href={"?alert=" + r.alert}>Open the September 2011 alert</a>.</p>
  <div id="receipt" data-alert={r.alert} data-revision={r.revision} data-sha256={r.sha256}>
    <p>Historical invoice totals from a UK online retailer show <strong>{r.delta}</strong> in net revenue above the weekday median. This retrospective alert identifies an unusual day. The aggregates cannot establish a cause or confirm fraud.</p>
    <h2>Rebuild the comparison</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Subtract credits from gross sales. <span class="equation">{r.gross} − {r.credits} = {r.actual}</span> recorded net revenue.</li>
      <li>Sort the {r.tuesdays} observed Tuesday net totals in the preceding twelve weeks. The middle two were {r.middle_low} and {r.middle_high}. Their mean is the weekday baseline of <strong>{r.expected}</strong>.</li>
      <li>Subtract the baseline from recorded net revenue. <span class="equation">{r.actual} − {r.expected} = {r.delta}</span>.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Where the difference came from</h2>
    <p>Each contribution is a country’s net sales on the alert date minus its share of the weekday baseline. The United Kingdom contributed <strong>{r.uk}</strong> of the deviation, the Netherlands <strong>{r.netherlands}</strong>, and the remaining countries <strong>{r.others}</strong> combined. These signed contributions sum to {r.delta}. Three decimal places preserve half-pennies in the baseline allocation.</p>
    <p>Source data from Daqing Chen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.24432/C5CG6D">Online Retail II, UCI Machine Learning Repository</a>. The public export contains aggregate values for this calculation.</p>
    <h2>Verify the released figures</h2>
    <p>Alert <code>{r.alert}</code><br>Compressed snapshot SHA-256 <code>{r.sha256}</code></p>
    <button type="button" class="btn" id="check-snapshot" hidden>Check snapshot checksum</button>
    <p id="check-result" role="status"></p>
    <p>For an independent, offline calculation, save the <a id="manifest" href="/signal-lab/snapshots/v2/manifest.json" download>release manifest</a>, <a id="snapshot" href={'/signal-lab/' + r.file} download>compressed snapshot</a> and <a href="verify.py" download>Python verifier</a> in one directory. Run this command with Python 3.</p>
    <p><code>python3 verify.py manifest.json {r.file.split('/').pop()}</code></p>
    <p>The <a href="https://github.com/brettadams0/brettadams0.github.io/tree/0fc79d95e010994d5567a966e49cc7c2b1b7be2c/signal-lab/snapshots">original published snapshot files</a> are pinned to portfolio revision <code>0fc79d9</code> for replay after a release change.</p>
    <p><a href="/signal-lab/#revenue">Explore the Revenue workspace</a></p>
  </div>

</div>
</Article>
<script is:inline>
(() => {
  const receipt = document.getElementById('receipt');
  const requested = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('alert');
  if (requested !== null && requested !== receipt.dataset.alert) {
    receipt.hidden = true;
    document.getElementById('missing-alert').hidden = false;
    return;
  }
  const button = document.getElementById('check-snapshot');
  const status = document.getElementById('check-result');
  button.hidden = false;
  button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    button.disabled = true;
    status.textContent = 'Checking the current public release…';
    try {
      const options = { cache: 'no-store', signal: AbortSignal.timeout(15000) };
      const manifest = await fetch(document.getElementById('manifest').href, options);
      if (!manifest.ok) throw new Error('fetch');
      const published = (await manifest.json()).financial?.revenue;
      const snapshotUrl = document.getElementById('snapshot').href;
      if (published?.revision !== receipt.dataset.revision || published.sha256 !== receipt.dataset.sha256 ||
          new URL(published.file, new URL('../../', manifest.url)).href !== snapshotUrl) {
        status.textContent = 'The current manifest no longer identifies this snapshot. The figures above describe the saved release only.';
        return;
      }
      const response = await fetch(snapshotUrl, options);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('fetch');
      const bytes = await response.arrayBuffer();
      const hash = new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', bytes));
      const digest = Array.from(hash, byte => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
      status.textContent = digest === receipt.dataset.sha256
        ? 'Verified. The downloaded bytes match the manifest and this investigation.'
        : 'Checksum mismatch. The downloaded bytes cannot verify this investigation.';
    } catch {
      status.textContent = 'Verification unavailable. Check your connection and retry, or run the Python verifier on previously saved files.';
    } finally {
      button.disabled = false;
    }
  });
})();
</script>

<style is:global>
  .investigation { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .investigation > * + * { margin-top: var(--s5); }
  .investigation h2 { margin-top: var(--s7); font-size: var(--fs-xl); color: var(--text); }
  .investigation ol { padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }
  .investigation .equation { font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--text); }
  .investigation [hidden] { display: none; }
  .investigation code { white-space: normal; }
  .investigation #receipt > * + * { margin-top: var(--s5); }
  .investigation #receipt > h2 + * { margin-top: var(--s3); }
</style>
